{% extends 'dashboard/help/_topic.html.twig' %}
{% block content %}
<p>catto-mail is installed from an exact <strong>release tag</strong> (for example <code>v0.2.0</code>), never from the moving <code>main</code> branch. Each release's notes and source downloads (zip and tar.gz with SHA-256 checksums) are on <a href="https://github.com/rrcatto/catto-mail/releases" rel="noopener noreferrer">the releases page</a>; the upgrade itself uses the Git tag, which is the same code.</p>
<pre class="cmd">cd ~/catto-mail
git fetch --tags
git tag --sort=-v:refname | head        # available releases
git describe --tags                     # the installed one
git checkout v0.2.2                     # the new release (read its CHANGELOG first)
infra/bin/smarthostctl prod check       # names any new setting you must add to infra/.env
infra/bin/smarthostctl prod upgrade 0.2.2</pre>
<p><code>prod upgrade</code> checks the running system, takes a backup, builds the new images, recreates the containers (migrations and grants run at start), and checks again. Then run all diagnostics.</p>
<h2>Rollback</h2>
<pre class="cmd">git checkout v0.2.0
infra/bin/smarthostctl prod rollback 0.2.0 &lt;the backup directory the upgrade made&gt;</pre>
<p>Rollback restores the previous images and the database from before the upgrade. Anything recorded after that backup is lost, so pause first and roll back promptly.</p>
{% endblock %}
